including the pre-auth-key path, which I had not covered in the issue. Two things unrelated to the logic.\n\n**1. The diff deletes an unrelated golden file and breaks a passing test.**\n\n`hscontrol/testdata/apiv1_golden/TestAPIV1ApiKeyDelete_path_prefix_with_id_query_is_both_->_400_parity.json` is removed. `assertAgainstGolden` hard-fails on a missing golden rather than regenerating, so:\n\n```\n$ go test ./hscontrol/ -run TestAPIV1ApiKeyDelete -count=1     # main\nok      github.com/juanfont/headscale/hscontrol 0.237s\n\n$ go test ./hscontrol/ -run TestAPIV1ApiKeyDelete -count=1     # 581cfd3\n--- FAIL: TestAPIV1ApiKeyDelete/path_prefix_with_id_query_is_both_->_400_parity\n    missing golden testdata/apiv1_golden/TestAPIV1ApiKeyDelete_path_prefix_with_id_query_is_both_->_400_parity.json\n    for DELETE /api/v1/apikey/... — run with HEADSCALE_UPDATE_GOLDEN=1 to generate\nFAIL\n```\n\nLooks like a stray `HEADSCALE_UPDATE_GOLDEN` run picking up a filename with `>` in it. Restoring the file should be the whole fix.\n\n**2. The new doc comment orphans the existing one.**\n\n`state.go:3001` onwards is now a single comment block, with the `isAutoDerivedGivenName` text ending up on `resyncAutoDerivedGivenName` and `isAutoDerivedGivenName` left undocumented:\n\n```go\n// isAutoDerivedGivenName reports whether given matches what\n// ... overwritten by client-side hostname changes).\n// resyncAutoDerivedGivenName mirrors the GivenName handling of\n// ...\nfunc resyncAutoDerivedGivenName(node *types.Node, newHostname string) {\n```\n\nNeeds a blank line and the original comment moved back down onto `isAutoDerivedGivenName`.\n\nI ran the Tailscale SaaS validation kradalby asked for and posted the full results on #3432. Short version, since it affects how this PR gets justified rather than whether it is correct: SaaS misses the resync on the reauth path exactly like headscale does, but converges on the next client start. So this PR converges earlier than SaaS and lands on the same end state, which is a better argument for it than the one I originally wrote in the issue.\n","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/comments/5434090667/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"Moep90","id":3042152,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMwNDIxNTI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3042152?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Moep90","html_url":"https://github.com/Moep90","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Moep90/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Moep90/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Moep90/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Moep90/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Moep90/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Moep90/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Moep90/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Moep90/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Moep90/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}}]